data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/d002-summary.md\", \"content\": \"# d002 report\\n\\n## What I implemented\\n\\n- `src/greet.py`: a `greet(name)` function returning `f\\\"Hello, {name}!\\\"`.\\n- `tests/test_greet.py`: unittest `TestCase` with two tests:\\n  - `test_normal_name`: asserts `greet(\\\"Alice\\\") == \\\"Hello, Alice!\\\"`\\n  - `test_empty_string`: asserts `greet(\\\"\\\") == \\\"Hello, !\\\"`\\n\\n## Test command and output\\n\\nRan from the repo root (`~/subject`):\\n\\n```\\n$ python3 -m unittest discover -s tests\\n..\\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\\nRan 2 tests in 0.000s\\n\\nOK\\n```\\n\\nExit code: `0` (confirmed via `echo $?`).\\n\\n## Commit\\n\\nCommitted both new files to the campaign branch\\n`cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>` (commit `f529927`), no other\\nbranch touched. Working tree is clean aside from `__pycache__` directories\\ngenerated by the test run, which were not staged/committed.\\n\\n## Issues\\n\\nNone. All steps in the dispatch completed and verified as described.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":1,"type":"content_block_delta"}

